# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the packaging changes that occurred with the release of Qiskit v1.0"
msgstr "Alamin ang mga pagbabago sa packaging na naganap nang ilabas ang Qiskit v1.0"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the breaking package changes"
msgstr "Alamin ang mga breaking na pagbabago sa package"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the breaking package changes {#understand-the-breaking-package-changes}"
msgstr "Alamin ang mga breaking na pagbabago sa package {#understand-the-breaking-package-changes}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit v1.0 uses a different packaging structure than previous Qiskit versions and will likely cause problems in environments that use packages that are not ready for Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang Qiskit v1.0 ng ibang istraktura ng packaging kaysa sa mga nakaraang bersyon ng Qiskit, at malamang na magdulot ito ng mga problema sa mga environment na gumagamit ng mga package na hindi pa handa para sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Do not try to upgrade an existing Python virtual environment to Qiskit v1.0 in-place. \n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Huwag subukang i-upgrade ang isang kasalukuyang Python virtual environment sa Qiskit v1.0 nang direkta (in-place).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will not make similar breaking packaging changes in the future. This is a one-time event, at the release of Qiskit v1.0, specifically so that our packaging story will be as easy as possible in the future.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi na kami gagawa ng mga katulad na breaking na pagbabago sa packaging sa hinaharap. Isang beses lang itong mangyayari, sa paglulunsad ng Qiskit v1.0, partikular na para maging mas simple ang aming packaging sa hinaharap.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This page contains detailed information about the pre-1.0 Qiskit package and why we made the breaking packaging changes.\n"
msgstr "Naglalaman ang pahinang ito ng detalyadong impormasyon tungkol sa pre-1.0 na Qiskit package at kung bakit namin ginawa ang mga breaking na pagbabago sa packaging.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We know that the change is inconvenient, but this restores Qiskit to the simple package structure that most Python packages use, which will be easier for users, developers, and library authors after the Qiskit v1.0 transition is complete.\n"
msgstr "Alam namin na nakakaabala ang pagbabago, ngunit ibinabalik nito ang Qiskit sa simpleng istraktura ng package na ginagamit ng karamihan sa mga Python package, na magiging mas madali para sa mga gumagamit, developer, at may-akda ng library pagkatapos makumpleto ang transisyon sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preface: glossary of Python packaging terminology {#preface-glossary-of-python-packaging-terminology}"
msgstr "Paunang salita: talasalitaan ng Python packaging terminology {#preface-glossary-of-python-packaging-terminology}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To better explain how the old Qiskit metapackage was structured and how that has changed with the release of Qiskit v1.0, below is a glossary of commonly used Python-packaging jargon. The following words have specific meanings that we'll use in this document.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"**Click to expand to read through this page's glossary**\">\n"
msgstr ""
"Para mas maipaliwanag kung paano nakaayos ang lumang Qiskit metapackage at kung paano ito nagbago sa paglulunsad ng Qiskit v1.0, narito ang isang talasalitaan ng mga karaniwang terminolohiya sa Python packaging. Ang mga sumusunod na salita ay may mga tiyak na kahulugan na gagamitin namin sa dokumentong ito.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"**I-click para palawakin at basahin ang talasalitaan ng pahinang ito**\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**module**: A single Python file.\n"
msgstr "**module**: Isang Python file.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**package**: A directory containing an `__init__.py` and other files or packages that Python can read.\n"
"This is the actual code as installed on your computer, and is what executes when you run `import something`.\n"
"Python considers any directory that is on the search path to be something you can import (and will import many additional items).\n"
msgstr ""
"**package**: Isang directory na naglalaman ng `__init__.py` at iba pang mga file o package na mababasa ng Python.\n"
"Ito ang aktwal na code na naka-install sa iyong computer, at ito ang nagpapatakbo kapag nag-run ka ng `import something`.\n"
"Itinuturing ng Python na maaari mong i-import ang anumang directory na nasa search path (at mag-iimport pa ng maraming karagdagang aytem).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This is not the same object that you `pip install` (which is a *distribution*), but typically what you `pip install` and what you `import` have the same name.\n"
msgstr "  Hindi ito ang parehong object na `pip install` mo (na isang *distribution*), ngunit karaniwan, ang `pip install` mo at ang `import` mo ay may parehong pangalan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**submodule**, **subpackage**: These are imprecise terms, but are commonly used.\n"
"The _sub_ part means \"contained inside a package\".\n"
"A submodule is a module and a subpackage is a package, but they are part of a larger package.\n"
msgstr ""
"**submodule**, **subpackage**: Mga hindi tiyak na termino, ngunit karaniwang ginagamit.\n"
"Ang bahaging _sub_ ay nangangahulugang \"nakapaloob sa isang package\".\n"
"Ang submodule ay isang module at ang subpackage ay isang package, ngunit bahagi sila ng isang mas malaking package.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**namespace package**: A package that can have submodules or subpackages installed into it by other _distributions_.\n"
"Critically, no one distribution contributing to a namespace package necessarily owns all the installed files, so it can be tricky to completely uninstall\n"
"or upgrade one.\n"
msgstr ""
"**namespace package**: Isang package na maaaring magkaroon ng mga submodule o subpackage na naka-install dito mula sa iba pang mga _distribution_.\n"
"Mahalagang tandaan: walang iisang distribution na nag-aambag sa isang namespace package ang tiyak na nagmamay-ari ng lahat ng naka-install na file, kaya maaaring maging mahirap ang ganap na pag-uninstall\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**distribution**: The compressed Python files, data files, and metadata that are downloaded when you run `pip install something`.\n"
"Often, a distribution contains exactly one package and the metadata about how to install it (its requirements and so on), but this is not required.\n"
"A distribution can contain zero or more modules or packages.\n"
msgstr ""
"**distribution**: Ang mga compressed na Python file, data file, at metadata na dina-download kapag nag-run ka ng `pip install something`.\n"
"Kadalasan, ang isang distribution ay naglalaman ng eksakto isang package at ang metadata tungkol sa kung paano ito i-install (ang mga kinakailangan nito at iba pa), ngunit hindi ito kinakailangan.\n"
"Ang isang distribution ay maaaring maglaman ng zero o higit pang mga module o package.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  If you are familiar with \"package managers\" outside the context of Python, such as `apt` from Debian/Ubuntu or Homebrew on macOS, then what they call a \"package\", Python calls a distribution, and there is no exact match for what Python calls a package.\n"
msgstr "  Kung pamilyar ka sa mga \"package manager\" sa labas ng konteksto ng Python, tulad ng `apt` mula sa Debian/Ubuntu o Homebrew sa macOS, kung gayon ang tinatawag nilang \"package\" ay tinatawag ng Python na distribution, at walang eksaktong katumbas para sa tinatawag ng Python na package.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Most sources talking about Python packaging use the term _package_ to mean both distributions and packages, and you must refer to the context to understand what is meant.\n"
"  In general, if you `import` it, the source means \"package\", and if you `pip install` it, the source means \"distribution\".\n"
msgstr ""
"  Karamihan sa mga pinagkukunan na nagsasalita tungkol sa Python packaging ay gumagamit ng terminong _package_ para mangahulugang parehong distribution at package, at kailangan mong sumangguni sa konteksto para maunawaan ang ibig sabihin.\n"
"  Sa pangkalahatan, kung `import` mo ito, ang ibig sabihin ng pinagkukunan ay \"package\", at kung `pip install` mo ito, ang ibig sabihin ng pinagkukunan ay \"distribution\".\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**search path**: When trying to `import something`, Python searches a predefined list of places for a module or package called `something`.\n"
"The list of places is the _search path_.\n"
"You can see and modify the search path in `sys.path`.\n"
msgstr ""
"**search path**: Kapag sinusubukang `import something`, naghahanap ang Python sa isang paunang natukoy na listahan ng mga lugar para sa isang module o package na tinatawag na `something`.\n"
"Ang listahan ng mga lugar ay ang _search path_.\n"
"Makikita at mababago mo ang search path sa `sys.path`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **requirement**: A distribution contains information on other distributions it depends on when installed.\n"
"  Any other distribution that is necessary is a _requirement_, and the package manager (usually `pip` or `conda`) should ensure that all requirements are installed with compatible versions.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"* **requirement**: Naglalaman ang isang distribution ng impormasyon tungkol sa iba pang distribution na inaasahan nito kapag naka-install.\n"
"  Ang anumang iba pang distribution na kinakailangan ay isang _requirement_, at ang package manager (karaniwan ay `pip` o `conda`) ay dapat tiyaking naka-install ang lahat ng requirement na may mga compatible na bersyon.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Python is highly dynamic, and many complexities can arise; for example, it's possible that a **module** or **package** does not correspond to files on disk, or that they are compiled extensions.\n"
msgstr "Napaka-dynamic ng Python, at maraming kumplikadong bagay ang maaaring lumabas; halimbawa, posible na ang isang **module** o **package** ay hindi tumutugma sa mga file sa disk, o na mga compiled na extension ang mga ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **search path** is not only a search over directories, but for this discussion, only files on disk are relevant.\n"
"Further complications aren't necessary to understand the problems described in this section, so you can use the model described above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **search path** ay hindi lamang isang paghahanap sa mga directory, ngunit para sa talakayan na ito, ang mga file lamang sa disk ang may kaugnayan.\n"
"Hindi na kailangan ng karagdagang kumplikadong bagay para maunawaan ang mga problemang inilarawan sa seksyong ito, kaya maaari mong gamitin ang modelong inilarawan sa itaas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The old Qiskit structure {#the-old-qiskit-structure}"
msgstr "Ang lumang istraktura ng Qiskit {#the-old-qiskit-structure}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Historically, Qiskit was comprised of many Python distributions: `qiskit-terra`, the compiler core; `qiskit-aer`, the high-performance simulator; the original IBM Quantum&reg; provider; and several now-obsolete packages providing particular exploratory algorithmic or experiment-running features.\n"
"For user ease, we also provided a Python distribution called `qiskit`, which contained no code of its own, but caused all the other components to be installed.\n"
"We called this the _metapackage_, by analogy to similar concepts in other package managers.\n"
"The code of the core of Qiskit lived in `qiskit-terra`, which owned the root of the Python package `qiskit`. In other words, `qiskit-terra` controlled what happened when you ran `import qiskit`.\n"
"Until Qiskit v1.0, the `qiskit` package was a namespace package and contained a second namespace package at `qiskit.providers`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kasaysayan, binubuo ang Qiskit ng maraming Python distribution: `qiskit-terra`, ang compiler core; `qiskit-aer`, ang high-performance simulator; ang orihinal na IBM Quantum&reg; provider; at ilang package na obsolete na ngayon na nagbibigay ng mga partikular na exploratory algorithmic o experiment-running na feature.\n"
"Para sa kaginhawahan ng gumagamit, nagbigay din kami ng Python distribution na tinatawag na `qiskit`, na walang sariling code, ngunit nag-install ng lahat ng iba pang component.\n"
"Tinawag namin ito na _metapackage_, sa pamamagitan ng pagkakatulad sa mga katulad na konsepto sa iba pang mga package manager.\n"
"Ang code ng core ng Qiskit ay nasa `qiskit-terra`, na nagmamay-ari ng root ng Python package na `qiskit`. Sa madaling salita, kontrolado ng `qiskit-terra` ang nangyayari kapag nag-run ka ng `import qiskit`.\n"
"Hanggang Qiskit v1.0, ang `qiskit` package ay isang namespace package at naglalaman ng pangalawang namespace package sa `qiskit.providers`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This organization caused us and our users quite a few problems.\n"
msgstr "Ang organisasyong ito ay nagdulot sa amin at sa aming mga gumagamit ng ilang mga problema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, downstream libraries that depended on Qiskit often only actually needed the compiler core, and did not require the rest of the large ecosystem that came with `pip install qiskit`.\n"
"They would therefore correctly specify their requirement as `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"However, when people tried to uninstall Qiskit by running `pip uninstall qiskit`, `pip` encountered problems:\n"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa, ang mga downstream library na umasa sa Qiskit ay kadalasan lang talaga kailangan ang compiler core, at hindi nangangailangan ng buong malaking ecosystem na kasama ng `pip install qiskit`.\n"
"Kaya tama nilang tinukoy ang kanilang requirement bilang `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"Ngunit, kapag sinubukan ng mga tao na i-uninstall ang Qiskit sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng `pip uninstall qiskit`, nakatagpo ng mga problema ang `pip`:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`pip` does not remove distributions that are now unused. So `pip uninstall qiskit` did almost nothing; there was no code in the distribution, so no code was removed.\n"
msgstr "Hindi inaalis ng `pip` ang mga distribution na hindi na ginagamit. Kaya ang `pip uninstall qiskit` ay halos walang ginawa; walang code sa distribution, kaya walang code na naalis.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Even if it were to remove code, many downstream distributions would remain installed because they depended on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr "Kahit na aalisin nito ang code, maraming downstream distribution ang mananatiling naka-install dahil umaasa sila sa `qiskit-terra`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Even if `qiskit-terra` was uninstalled, it might still leave an importable `qiskit` directory with no usable code, because it was a namespace package.\n"
msgstr "Kahit na na-uninstall ang `qiskit-terra`, maaari pa ring mag-iwan ito ng importable na `qiskit` directory na walang magamit na code, dahil ito ay isang namespace package.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When installing or upgrading distributions with a `pip install` command, `pip` also does not take into account previous requirement resolutions.\n"
"Because there were two packages, upgrading a package that required `qiskit-terra` to be upgraded caused an invalid environment; `pip` upgraded `qiskit-terra` but left `qiskit` untouched.\n"
"It issued a warning on this and all subsequent `pip install` commands, but because nothing appeared broken, users typically ignored the warning, and `pip` did not raise an error status or forbid operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nag-install o nag-upgrade ng mga distribution gamit ang isang `pip install` command, hindi rin isinasaalang-alang ng `pip` ang mga nakaraang resolution ng requirement.\n"
"Dahil may dalawang package, ang pag-upgrade ng isang package na nangangailangan ng pag-upgrade ng `qiskit-terra` ay nagdulot ng invalid na environment; na-upgrade ng `pip` ang `qiskit-terra` ngunit hindi nito hinawakan ang `qiskit`.\n"
"Nagbigay ito ng babala sa nito at sa lahat ng kasunod na `pip install` command, ngunit dahil walang tila nabasag, karaniwan ay hindi pinansin ng mga gumagamit ang babala, at hindi nagtaas ng error status o nagbawal ng mga operasyon ang `pip`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Over time, we removed elements from the `qiskit` metapackage until, starting with Qiskit v0.44, only `qiskit-terra` remains.\n"
"Of these components, `qiskit-aer` still exists and is actively updated, but it is now installed as a separate distribution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa paglipas ng panahon, inalis namin ang mga elemento mula sa `qiskit` metapackage hanggang, simula sa Qiskit v0.44, `qiskit-terra` na lang ang natitira.\n"
"Sa mga component na ito, ang `qiskit-aer` ay umiiral pa rin at aktibong ina-update, ngunit ito ngayon ay naka-install bilang isang hiwalay na distribution.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, we ever more strongly discouraged other libraries from using the namespace hooks.\n"
"We removed the last Qiskit use of the hooks in non-obsolete packages with the release of Qiskit Aer v0.11 and its new `qiskit_aer` Python package, although until Qiskit v1.0 we also forced the namespace path `qiskit.providers.aer` to work.\n"
"Starting with Qiskit v1.0, we have removed the ability for packages to extend any `qiskit` namespace. Thus, `pip uninstall` on the correct distribution in a valid environment now works as expected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayundin, lalo na naming hinimok ang iba pang mga library na huwag gumamit ng namespace hooks.\n"
"Inalis namin ang huling paggamit ng Qiskit ng mga hook sa mga hindi-obsolete na package sa paglulunsad ng Qiskit Aer v0.11 at ang bagong `qiskit_aer` Python package nito, kahit hanggang Qiskit v1.0 ay pinilit pa rin naming gumana ang namespace path na `qiskit.providers.aer`.\n"
"Simula sa Qiskit v1.0, inalis na namin ang kakayahan ng mga package na palawakin ang anumang `qiskit` namespace. Kaya, ang `pip uninstall` sa tamang distribution sa isang valid na environment ngayon ay gumagana na tulad ng inaasahan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The new Qiskit structure {#the-new-qiskit-structure}"
msgstr "Ang bagong istraktura ng Qiskit {#the-new-qiskit-structure}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Starting with version 1.0, Qiskit comprises a single distribution, called `qiskit`, which installs one single package, also called `qiskit`, which owns all the code contained in its directory.\n"
"This is the normal structure of Python code, and is the simplest and least error-prone structure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Simula sa bersyon 1.0, ang Qiskit ay binubuo ng isang distribution, na tinatawag na `qiskit`, na nag-iinstall ng isang package, na tinatawag din na `qiskit`, na nagmamay-ari ng lahat ng code na nakapaloob sa directory nito.\n"
"Ito ang normal na istraktura ng Python code, at ito ang pinakasimple at pinaka-hindi-nagkakamaling istraktura.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `qiskit-terra` distribution on PyPI will never be updated to version 1.0 or beyond; it is entirely superseded by `qiskit`.\n"
"The name `qiskit-terra` is no longer involved in the installation.\n"
"However, the `qiskit-terra` package is not being removed from PyPI, and we will leave its most recent version in a working state, so old scientific code and legacy packages can more easily continue to use it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `qiskit-terra` distribution sa PyPI ay hindi na ia-update sa bersyon 1.0 o higit pa; ganap itong pinalitan ng `qiskit`.\n"
"Ang pangalang `qiskit-terra` ay hindi na kasangkot sa pag-install.\n"
"Ngunit, ang `qiskit-terra` package ay hindi inaalis mula sa PyPI, at iiwanan namin ang pinakabagong bersyon nito sa isang gumaganang estado, para mas madaling magpatuloy itong gamitin ng lumang scientific code at legacy package.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, because of the metapackage legacy and deficiencies in `pip` as a package manager, it is not possible for us to make a completely smooth upgrade path for users to Qiskit v1.0, especially while some packages depend on earlier versions of Qiskit, and some require only Qiskit v1.0+.\n"
"These problems will lessen as more of the ecosystem migrates to Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kasamaang-palad, dahil sa legacy ng metapackage at mga kakulangan sa `pip` bilang isang package manager, hindi posible para sa amin na gumawa ng ganap na maayos na upgrade path para sa mga gumagamit patungo sa Qiskit v1.0, lalo na habang ang ilang mga package ay umaasa sa mga mas lumang bersyon ng Qiskit, at ang ilan ay nangangailangan ng Qiskit v1.0+ lamang.\n"
"Ang mga problemang ito ay mababawasan habang mas maraming ecosystem ang nag-migrate sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where did the application modules go? {#where-did-the-application-modules-go}"
msgstr "Nasaan na ang mga application module? {#where-did-the-application-modules-go}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You may notice that the command `pip install qiskit` will no longer includes packages such as `qiskit-aer` or `qiskit-nature`. With the removal of the metapackage structure, many of these packages were split into distributions that need to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong mapansin na ang command na `pip install qiskit` ay hindi na nagsasama ng mga package tulad ng `qiskit-aer` o `qiskit-nature`. Sa pag-alis ng metapackage structure, marami sa mga package na ito ay nahahati sa mga distribution na kailangang i-install nang hiwalay.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit was comprised of many different Python distributions, such as `qiskit-terra`, the compiler core; `qiskit-aer`, the high-performance simulator; the original IBM Quantum&reg; provider; and several now-obsolete packages providing particular exploratory algorithmic or experiment-running features.\n"
msgstr "Bago ang paglulunsad ng Qiskit SDK v1.0, ang Qiskit ay binubuo ng maraming iba't ibang Python distribution, tulad ng `qiskit-terra`, ang compiler core; `qiskit-aer`, ang high-performance simulator; ang orihinal na IBM Quantum&reg; provider; at ilang package na obsolete na ngayon na nagbibigay ng mga partikular na exploratory algorithmic o experiment-running na feature.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you want to install the packages that were previously included in the Qiskit metapackage, visit the [Qiskit ecosystem](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) to find a range of packages to suit your needs. You can also read the [v1.0 migration guide](/guides/qiskit-1.0-installation) for more information about how to install the new distribution.\n"
msgstr "Kung gusto mong i-install ang mga package na dating kasama sa Qiskit metapackage, bisitahin ang [Qiskit ecosystem](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) para mahanap ang iba't ibang mga package na angkop sa iyong mga pangangailangan. Maaari ka ring basahin ang [v1.0 migration guide](/guides/qiskit-1.0-installation) para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa kung paano i-install ang bagong distribution.\n"
